msgid "Dictionary and Path Classes"
msgstr "Classes de dictionnaire et de chemins"

msgid ""
"This module provides tools and class for creating nested dictionaries, "
"since standard python does not have nested dictionaries."
msgstr ""
"Ce module fournit des outils et une classe pour créer des dictionnaires "
"imbriqués, puisque Python standard n’a pas de dictionnaires imbriqués."

msgid "Dictionary classes"
msgstr "Classes de dictionnaire"

msgid "Nested dictionary class."
msgstr "Classe de dictionnaire imbriqué."

msgid ""
"This class is designed as a stacked dictionary. It represents a nest of "
"dictionaries, that is to say that each key is a value or a nested "
"dictionary. And so on..."
msgstr ""
"Cette classe est conçue comme un dictionnaire empilé. Elle représente un "
"emboîtement de dictionnaires, c’est-à-dire que chaque clé est une valeur "
"ou un dictionnaire imbriqué. Et ainsi de suite…"

msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "Paramètres"

msgid "Initial data. Nested plain dictionaries are converted recursively."
msgstr ""
"Données initiales. Les dictionnaires simples imbriqués sont convertis "
"récursivement."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Configuration (keyword-only) with 'indent' and 'default_factory' keys. "
"When omitted or empty, ``{'indent': 0, 'default_factory': "
"NestedDictionary}`` is used. To get strict behaviour, use "
"``StrictNestedDictionary`` or pass ``'default_factory': None``."
msgstr ""
"Configuration (argument nommé uniquement) avec les clés 'indent' et "
"'default_factory'. Lorsqu’elle est omise ou vide, ``{'indent': 0, "
"'default_factory': NestedDictionary}`` est utilisée. Pour obtenir un "
"comportement strict, utilisez ``StrictNestedDictionary`` ou passez "
"``'default_factory': None``."

msgid ""
"Initial data given as keyword arguments. They are data, not settings: "
"``NestedDictionary(indent=2)`` creates a key ``'indent'``."
msgstr ""
"Données initiales fournies comme arguments nommés. Ce sont des données, "
"pas des réglages : ``NestedDictionary(indent=2)`` crée une clé "
"``'indent'``."

msgid "Examples"
msgstr "Exemples"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> # From a dictionary\n"
">>> nd1 = NestedDictionary({'first': 1, 'second': {'1': \"2:1\", '2': "
"\"2:2\"}, 'third': 3})\n"
">>> nd1['second']['2']\n"
"'2:2'"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> # À partir d’un dictionnaire\n"
">>> nd1 = NestedDictionary({'first': 1, 'second': {'1': \"2:1\", '2': "
"\"2:2\"}, 'third': 3})\n"
">>> nd1['second']['2']\n"
"'2:2'"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # From an iterable of (key, value) pairs\n"
">>> nd2 = NestedDictionary(zip(['first', 'second', 'third'],\n"
"...                            [1, {'1': \"2:1\", '2': \"2:2\"}, 3]))\n"
">>> nd3 = NestedDictionary([('first', 1), ('second', {'1': \"2:1\", '2': "
"\"2:2\"}),\n"
"...                         ('third', 3)])\n"
">>> nd1 == nd2 == nd3\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> # À partir d’un itérable de paires (clé, valeur)\n"
">>> nd2 = NestedDictionary(zip(['first', 'second', 'third'],\n"
"...                            [1, {'1': \"2:1\", '2': \"2:2\"}, 3]))\n"
">>> nd3 = NestedDictionary([('first', 1), ('second', {'1': \"2:1\", '2': "
"\"2:2\"}),\n"
"...                         ('third', 3)])\n"
">>> nd1 == nd2 == nd3\n"
"True"

msgid ""
">>> # Nested plain dictionaries become NestedDictionary levels\n"
">>> type(nd1['second']).__name__\n"
"'NestedDictionary'"
msgstr ""
">>> # Les dictionnaires simples imbriqués deviennent des niveaux "
"NestedDictionary\n"
">>> type(nd1['second']).__name__\n"
"'NestedDictionary'"

msgid "Get a view of all hierarchical paths in this dictionary."
msgstr "Renvoie une vue de tous les chemins hiérarchiques de ce dictionnaire."

msgid ""
"Returns a lazy view over all paths without storing them in memory. The "
"view supports iteration, length queries, membership tests, and various "
"path operations."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie une vue paresseuse de tous les chemins, sans les stocker en "
"mémoire. La vue permet l’itération, le calcul de la longueur, les tests "
"d’appartenance et diverses opérations sur les chemins."

msgid "Returns"
msgstr "Renvoie"

msgid "A lazy view over all paths in the nested dictionary"
msgstr "Une vue paresseuse de tous les chemins du dictionnaire imbriqué"

msgid "Return type"
msgstr "Type renvoyé"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> paths = nd.paths()\n"
">>> list(paths)\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> paths = nd.paths()\n"
">>> list(paths)\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"

msgid ""
">>> # Check if path exists\n"
">>> ['a', 'b'] in paths\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> # Teste si un chemin existe\n"
">>> ['a', 'b'] in paths\n"
"True"

msgid ""
">>> # Get number of paths\n"
">>> len(paths)\n"
"4"
msgstr ""
">>> # Nombre de chemins\n"
">>> len(paths)\n"
"4"

msgid ""
">>> # Get children of a path\n"
">>> paths.get_children(['a'])\n"
"['b', 'c']"
msgstr ""
">>> # Enfants d’un chemin\n"
">>> paths.get_children(['a'])\n"
"['b', 'c']"

msgid ":py:obj:`compact_paths`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`compact_paths`"

msgid "Get compact representation of paths"
msgstr "Renvoie la représentation compacte des chemins"

msgid ":py:obj:`PathsView`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`PathsView`"

msgid "Documentation of the paths view class"
msgstr "Documentation de la classe de vue des chemins"

msgid "Get a compact representation of all paths in this dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie une représentation compacte de tous les chemins de ce "
"dictionnaire."

msgid ""
"Returns a compact view where the hierarchical structure is represented as"
" nested lists, providing a factorized representation of paths."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie une vue compacte où la structure hiérarchique est représentée par"
" des listes imbriquées, ce qui donne une représentation factorisée des "
"chemins."

msgid "A compact view with factorized path structure"
msgstr "Une vue compacte à la structure de chemins factorisée"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> cpaths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> cpaths.structure\n"
"[['a', 'b', 'c'], 'd']"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> cpaths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> cpaths.structure\n"
"[['a', 'b', 'c'], 'd']"

msgid ""
">>> # Expand to full paths\n"
">>> cpaths.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"
msgstr ""
">>> # Développe en chemins complets\n"
">>> cpaths.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"

msgid ""
">>> # Check coverage\n"
">>> cpaths.is_covering(nd)\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> # Vérifie la couverture\n"
">>> cpaths.is_covering(nd)\n"
"True"

msgid ":py:obj:`paths`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`paths`"

msgid "Get standard paths view"
msgstr "Renvoie la vue standard des chemins"

msgid ":py:obj:`CompactPathsView`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`CompactPathsView`"

msgid "Documentation of the compact paths view class"
msgstr "Documentation de la classe de vue des chemins compacts"

msgid "Find the hierarchical path (ancestors) leading to a specific value."
msgstr "Trouve le chemin hiérarchique (les ancêtres) qui mène à une valeur donnée."

msgid ""
"Searches the nested structure for the given value and returns the "
"complete path of keys leading to it, excluding the final key. This "
"returns the \"ancestry\" of the value in the tree."
msgstr ""
"Parcourt la structure imbriquée à la recherche de la valeur donnée et "
"renvoie le chemin complet des clés qui y mène, sans la clé finale. Cela "
"renvoie l’« ascendance » de la valeur dans l’arbre."

msgid "Value to search for in the nested dictionary"
msgstr "Valeur à rechercher dans le dictionnaire imbriqué"

msgid "list of keys forming the path to the value (excluding final key)"
msgstr "liste des clés formant le chemin vers la valeur (sans la clé finale)"

msgid "Raises"
msgstr "Lève"

msgid "If value is not found in the dictionary"
msgstr "Si la valeur est absente du dictionnaire"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}})\n"
">>> nd.ancestors(1)\n"
"['a', 'b']"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}})\n"
">>> nd.ancestors(1)\n"
"['a', 'b']"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': {'d': 2}})\n"
">>> nd.ancestors(2)\n"
"['c']"
msgstr ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': {'d': 2}})\n"
">>> nd.ancestors(2)\n"
"['c']"

msgid ""
">>> nd.ancestors(999)\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedValueError: Value 999 not found in the "
"dictionary..."
msgstr ""
">>> nd.ancestors(999)\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedValueError: Value 999 not found in the "
"dictionary..."

msgid "Notes"
msgstr "Notes"

msgid "Returns path excluding the final key (direct parent of value)"
msgstr "Renvoie le chemin sans la clé finale (parent direct de la valeur)"

msgid "Uses DFS to find the first occurrence"
msgstr "Utilise un parcours en profondeur pour trouver la première occurrence"

msgid "If value appears multiple times, returns first found path"
msgstr "Si la valeur apparaît plusieurs fois, renvoie le premier chemin trouvé"

msgid "Empty list returned for top-level values"
msgstr "Une liste vide est renvoyée pour les valeurs de premier niveau"

msgid ":py:obj:`dfs`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`dfs`"

msgid "Depth-first traversal"
msgstr "Parcours en profondeur"

msgid ":py:obj:`unpacked_items`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`unpacked_items`"

msgid "Get all (path, value) pairs"
msgstr "Renvoie toutes les paires (chemin, valeur)"

msgid "Breadth-first traversal of the terminal values."
msgstr "Parcours en largeur des valeurs terminales."

msgid ""
"Walks the dictionary level by level with a queue, and yields the keys "
"whose value is not a nested dictionary, with their path: all those of "
"depth N before those of depth N+1. Keys whose value is a nested "
"dictionary are traversed but not yielded, so an empty nested dictionary "
"yields nothing."
msgstr ""
"Parcourt le dictionnaire niveau par niveau à l’aide d’une file, et "
"produit les clés dont la valeur n’est pas un dictionnaire imbriqué, avec "
"leur chemin : toutes celles de profondeur N avant celles de profondeur "
"N+1. Les clés dont la valeur est un dictionnaire imbriqué sont parcourues"
" mais pas produites ; un dictionnaire imbriqué vide ne produit donc rien."

msgid "Yields"
msgstr "Produit"

msgid ""
"*tuple* -- (path_tuple, value) for each terminal value, in breadth-first "
"order"
msgstr ""
"*tuple* -- (path_tuple, valeur) pour chaque valeur terminale, dans "
"l’ordre du parcours en largeur"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}})\n"
">>> list(nd.bfs())\n"
"[(('a', 'b', 'c'), 1)]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}})\n"
">>> list(nd.bfs())\n"
"[(('a', 'b', 'c'), 1)]"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> list(nd.bfs())\n"
"[(('d',), 3), (('a', 'b'), 1), (('a', 'c'), 2)]"
msgstr ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> list(nd.bfs())\n"
"[(('d',), 3), (('a', 'b'), 1), (('a', 'c'), 2)]"

msgid ""
"Yields terminal values only, unlike :meth:`dfs`, which also yields the "
"keys whose value is a nested dictionary"
msgstr ""
"Ne produit que les valeurs terminales, contrairement à :meth:`dfs`, qui "
"produit aussi les clés dont la valeur est un dictionnaire imbriqué"

msgid "Returns paths as immutable tuples"
msgstr "Renvoie les chemins sous forme de tuples immuables"

msgid "Create a shallow copy of the nested dictionary."
msgstr "Crée une copie superficielle du dictionnaire imbriqué."

msgid "Shallow copy of the same class, with the same configuration"
msgstr "Copie superficielle de la même classe, avec la même configuration"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd2 = nd.copy()\n"
">>> nd2['a'] is nd['a']\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd2 = nd.copy()\n"
">>> nd2['a'] is nd['a']\n"
"True"

msgid ":py:obj:`__copy__`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`__copy__`"

msgid "Internal implementation"
msgstr "Implémentation interne"

msgid ":py:obj:`deepcopy`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`deepcopy`"

msgid "Create independent copy"
msgstr "Crée une copie indépendante"

msgid "Create a deep copy of the nested dictionary."
msgstr "Crée une copie profonde du dictionnaire imbriqué."

msgid ""
"Creates a completely independent copy where all nested structures and "
"mutable leaf values are recursively duplicated. Equivalent to "
"``copy.deepcopy(self)``."
msgstr ""
"Crée une copie entièrement indépendante, dans laquelle toutes les "
"structures imbriquées et les valeurs terminales mutables sont dupliquées "
"récursivement. Équivalent à ``copy.deepcopy(self)``."

msgid "Complete independent copy of the same class"
msgstr "Copie entièrement indépendante de la même classe"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd2 = nd.deepcopy()\n"
">>> nd2['a']['b'] = 999\n"
">>> nd['a']['b']\n"
"1"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd2 = nd.deepcopy()\n"
">>> nd2['a']['b'] = 999\n"
">>> nd['a']['b']\n"
"1"

msgid ":py:obj:`__deepcopy__`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`__deepcopy__`"

msgid ":py:obj:`copy`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`copy`"

msgid "Shallow copy alternative"
msgstr "Alternative par copie superficielle"

msgid "Get configuration as an ordered list of (key, value) tuples."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie la configuration sous forme de liste ordonnée de tuples (clé, "
"valeur)."

msgid ""
"Returns a deterministic view of the internal configuration with priority "
"ordering: 'indent', 'default_factory', then alphabetically."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie une vue déterministe de la configuration interne, dans un ordre "
"de priorité : 'indent', 'default_factory', puis par ordre alphabétique."

msgid "Configuration as [(key, value), ...] in priority order"
msgstr "Configuration sous la forme [(clé, valeur), ...] dans l’ordre de priorité"

msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary()\n"
">>> nd.default_setup\n"
"[('indent', 0), ('default_factory', <class "
"'ndict_tools.core.NestedDictionary'>)]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary()\n"
">>> nd.default_setup\n"
"[('indent', 0), ('default_factory', <class "
"'ndict_tools.core.NestedDictionary'>)]"

msgid ":py:obj:`default_setup.setter`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`default_setup.setter`"

msgid "set new configuration"
msgstr "définit une nouvelle configuration"

msgid "Depth-First Search traversal of the nested dictionary."
msgstr "Parcours en profondeur du dictionnaire imbriqué."

msgid ""
"Recursively traverses the dictionary in depth-first order, yielding each "
"hierarchical path (as list) and its corresponding value. This includes "
"both intermediate nodes and leaf values."
msgstr ""
"Parcourt récursivement le dictionnaire en profondeur, en produisant "
"chaque chemin hiérarchique (sous forme de liste) et la valeur "
"correspondante. Cela inclut à la fois les nœuds intermédiaires et les "
"valeurs des feuilles."

msgid "Current node being traversed (defaults to root/self)"
msgstr "Nœud courant parcouru (par défaut la racine, self)"

msgid "Current path being constructed (defaults to empty list)"
msgstr "Chemin courant en construction (par défaut une liste vide)"

msgid "*tuple* -- (path_list, value) for each node in DFS order"
msgstr ""
"*tuple* -- (path_list, valeur) pour chaque nœud, dans l’ordre du parcours"
" en profondeur"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> for path, value in nd.dfs():\n"
"...     if isinstance(value, NestedDictionary):\n"
"...         value = value.to_dict()\n"
"...     print(path, value)\n"
"['a'] {'b': 1}\n"
"['a', 'b'] 1\n"
"['c'] 2"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> for path, value in nd.dfs():\n"
"...     if isinstance(value, NestedDictionary):\n"
"...         value = value.to_dict()\n"
"...     print(path, value)\n"
"['a'] {'b': 1}\n"
"['a', 'b'] 1\n"
"['c'] 2"

msgid "Visits nodes before their children (pre-order)"
msgstr "Visite les nœuds avant leurs enfants (ordre préfixe)"

msgid "Returns paths as mutable lists (unlike unpacked_keys)"
msgstr ""
"Renvoie les chemins sous forme de listes mutables (contrairement à "
"unpacked_keys)"

msgid "Includes intermediate dictionary nodes"
msgstr "Inclut les nœuds intermédiaires de type dictionnaire"

msgid "Useful for tree-based operations"
msgstr "Utile pour les opérations sur les arbres"

msgid ":py:obj:`bfs`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`bfs`"

msgid "Breadth-first traversal"
msgstr "Parcours en largeur"

msgid "Similar but only terminal values"
msgstr "Semblable, mais seulement les valeurs terminales"

msgid "Check equality: same class, configuration, and content."
msgstr "Teste l’égalité : même classe, même configuration et même contenu."

msgid ""
"Two nested dictionaries are equal if they have: 1. Identical class type "
"(exact match, not subclasses) 2. Identical default_setup configuration 3."
" Identical dictionary structure and values"
msgstr ""
"Deux dictionnaires imbriqués sont égaux s’ils ont : 1. exactement la même"
" classe (pas une sous-classe) 2. la même configuration default_setup 3. "
"la même structure et les mêmes valeurs"

msgid "This is the strictest comparison, and the one used by ``==``."
msgstr "C’est la comparaison la plus stricte, et celle qu’utilise ``==``."

msgid "Object to compare with"
msgstr "Objet à comparer"

msgid "True if all conditions met"
msgstr "True si toutes les conditions sont remplies"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd1 = NestedDictionary({'a': 1})\n"
">>> nd2 = NestedDictionary({'a': 1})\n"
">>> nd1.equal(nd2)\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd1 = NestedDictionary({'a': 1})\n"
">>> nd2 = NestedDictionary({'a': 1})\n"
">>> nd1.equal(nd2)\n"
"True"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # Different setup\n"
">>> nd3 = NestedDictionary(\n"
"...     {'a': 1},\n"
"...     default_setup={'indent': 4, 'default_factory': NestedDictionary},"
"\n"
"... )\n"
">>> nd1.equal(nd3)\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> # Configuration différente\n"
">>> nd3 = NestedDictionary(\n"
"...     {'a': 1},\n"
"...     default_setup={'indent': 4, 'default_factory': NestedDictionary},"
"\n"
"... )\n"
">>> nd1.equal(nd3)\n"
"False"

msgid ":py:obj:`__eq__`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`__eq__`"

msgid "Same as equal"
msgstr "Identique à equal"

msgid ":py:obj:`__ne__`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`__ne__`"

msgid "Inequality check"
msgstr "Test d’inégalité"

msgid ":py:obj:`isomorph`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`isomorph`"

msgid "Same content, any class of the family"
msgstr "Même contenu, toute classe de la famille"

msgid ":py:obj:`similar`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`similar`"

msgid "Same content only"
msgstr "Même contenu seulement"

msgid ""
"Recursively convert a standard dictionary to a nested dictionary of this "
"class."
msgstr ""
"Convertit récursivement un dictionnaire standard en dictionnaire imbriqué"
" de cette classe."

msgid ""
"Alternative constructor that transforms a regular nested dictionary into "
"an instance of the class it is called on. The target class is ``cls`` "
"itself, eliminating the need to pass the class explicitly and preventing "
"errors in recursive calls."
msgstr ""
"Constructeur alternatif qui transforme un dictionnaire imbriqué ordinaire"
" en instance de la classe sur laquelle il est appelé. La classe cible est"
" ``cls`` elle-même, ce qui évite de passer la classe explicitement et "
"prévient les erreurs dans les appels récursifs."

msgid "The dictionary to transform (may be nested)."
msgstr "Le dictionnaire à transformer (éventuellement imbriqué)."

msgid ""
"Initialization options, passed to ``cls`` at every level. "
"``default_setup`` is optional: as for the constructor, the configuration "
"is resolved by ``cls._normalize_setup``, which supplies the default of "
"the class when none is given."
msgstr ""
"Options d’initialisation, passées à ``cls`` à chaque niveau. "
"``default_setup`` est facultatif : comme pour le constructeur, la "
"configuration est résolue par ``cls._normalize_setup``, qui fournit la "
"configuration par défaut de la classe lorsqu’aucune n’est donnée."

msgid "New instance of the calling class containing the dictionary structure."
msgstr ""
"Nouvelle instance de la classe appelante contenant la structure du "
"dictionnaire."

msgid ""
"If ``default_setup`` is missing and ``cls`` defines no default     "
"configuration."
msgstr ""
"Si ``default_setup`` est absent et que ``cls`` ne définit aucune "
"configuration par défaut."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary.from_dict({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd['a']['b']\n"
"1\n"
">>> strict = NestedDictionary.from_dict(\n"
"...     {'a': {'b': 1}},\n"
"...     default_setup={'indent': 0, 'default_factory': None}\n"
"... )"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary.from_dict({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd['a']['b']\n"
"1\n"
">>> strict = NestedDictionary.from_dict(\n"
"...     {'a': {'b': 1}},\n"
"...     default_setup={'indent': 0, 'default_factory': None}\n"
"... )"

msgid ""
"Values that are already nested dictionaries of the family are preserved "
"as-is."
msgstr ""
"Les valeurs qui sont déjà des dictionnaires imbriqués de la famille sont "
"conservées telles quelles."

msgid "Regular ``dict`` values are recursively converted using ``cls``."
msgstr ""
"Les valeurs ``dict`` ordinaires sont converties récursivement avec "
"``cls``."

msgid "Non-dict values are assigned directly."
msgstr "Les valeurs qui ne sont pas des dictionnaires sont affectées directement."

msgid ":py:obj:`to_dict`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`to_dict`"

msgid "Inverse operation."
msgstr "Opération inverse."

msgid "Reconstruct a nested dictionary of this class from a JSON file."
msgstr ""
"Reconstruit un dictionnaire imbriqué de cette classe à partir d’un "
"fichier JSON."

msgid ""
"Keys written in square brackets by ``to_json`` are decoded back to their "
"original Python types; escaped string keys lose their escape. Round-trips"
" are lossless for supported types: ``str``, ``int``, ``float``, ``bool``,"
" flat ``tuple``, flat ``frozenset``."
msgstr ""
"Les clés écrites entre crochets par ``to_json`` sont décodées vers leur "
"type Python d’origine ; les clés chaînes échappées perdent leur "
"échappement. L’aller-retour est sans perte pour les types pris en charge "
": ``str``, ``int``, ``float``, ``bool``, ``tuple`` plat, ``frozenset`` "
"plat."

msgid "Path to the JSON file."
msgstr "Chemin du fichier JSON."

msgid ""
"Passed to ``cls.from_dict``. The JSON file carries no configuration: "
"``default_setup`` gives it, and when it is absent "
"``cls._normalize_setup`` supplies the default of the class."
msgstr ""
"Passé à ``cls.from_dict``. Le fichier JSON ne contient aucune "
"configuration : ``default_setup`` la fournit et, en son absence, "
"``cls._normalize_setup`` fournit la configuration par défaut de la "
"classe."

msgid "Reconstructed instance of the calling class."
msgstr "Instance reconstruite de la classe appelante."

msgid ""
"If the root of the JSON document is not an object (for example a     list"
" or a scalar), so no instance of the calling class is built."
msgstr ""
"Si la racine du document JSON n’est pas un objet (par exemple une liste "
"ou un scalaire), si bien qu’aucune instance de la classe appelante n’est "
"construite."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> import tempfile\n"
">>> from pathlib import Path\n"
">>> tmp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n"
">>> path = Path(tmp.name) / 'nd.json'\n"
">>> NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}}).to_json(path)\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary.from_json(path)\n"
">>> nd.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}}\n"
">>> strict = NestedDictionary.from_json(\n"
"...     path,\n"
"...     default_setup={'indent': 0, 'default_factory': None}\n"
"... )\n"
">>> strict.default_factory is None\n"
"True\n"
">>> tmp.cleanup()"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> import tempfile\n"
">>> from pathlib import Path\n"
">>> tmp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n"
">>> path = Path(tmp.name) / 'nd.json'\n"
">>> NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}}).to_json(path)\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary.from_json(path)\n"
">>> nd.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}}\n"
">>> strict = NestedDictionary.from_json(\n"
"...     path,\n"
"...     default_setup={'indent': 0, 'default_factory': None}\n"
"... )\n"
">>> strict.default_factory is None\n"
"True\n"
">>> tmp.cleanup()"

msgid ":py:obj:`to_json`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`to_json`"

msgid "Serialize to a JSON file."
msgstr "Sérialise dans un fichier JSON."

msgid "Reconstruct a nested dictionary of this class from a pickle file."
msgstr ""
"Reconstruit un dictionnaire imbriqué de cette classe à partir d’un "
"fichier pickle."

msgid "Path to the pickle file."
msgstr "Chemin du fichier pickle."

msgid "If ``True`` (default), verify the SHA-256 sidecar before loading."
msgstr ""
"Si ``True`` (par défaut), vérifie le fichier d’empreinte SHA-256 avant le"
" chargement."

msgid ""
"Not used directly (the pickled object carries its own state), but "
"accepted for API symmetry with ``from_json``."
msgstr ""
"Non utilisé directement (l’objet enregistré porte son propre état), mais "
"accepté par symétrie d’API avec ``from_json``."

msgid ""
"Reconstructed instance. The pickled object keeps its own class, which is "
"the calling class or one of its subclasses."
msgstr ""
"Instance reconstruite. L’objet enregistré conserve sa propre classe, qui "
"est la classe appelante ou l’une de ses sous-classes."

msgid "If ``verify=True`` and the digest mismatches or sidecar is absent."
msgstr ""
"Si ``verify=True`` et que l’empreinte ne correspond pas ou que le fichier"
" d’empreinte est absent."

msgid ""
"If the pickled object is not an instance of the calling class, for     "
"example a ``NestedDictionary`` file loaded with     "
"``StrictNestedDictionary.from_pickle``."
msgstr ""
"Si l’objet enregistré n’est pas une instance de la classe appelante, par "
"exemple un fichier ``NestedDictionary`` chargé avec "
"``StrictNestedDictionary.from_pickle``."

msgid "Warns"
msgstr "Avertissements"

msgid "**UserWarning** -- Pickle is unsafe with untrusted files."
msgstr "**UserWarning** -- Pickle n’est pas sûr avec des fichiers non fiables."

msgid ":py:obj:`to_pickle`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`to_pickle`"

msgid "Serialize to a pickle file."
msgstr "Sérialise dans un fichier pickle."

msgid "Compute the number of levels of the nested structure."
msgstr "Calcule le nombre de niveaux de la structure imbriquée."

msgid ""
"This is the number of keys on the longest path. Top-level keys have depth"
" 0, so the result is the greatest depth of a key plus 1. An empty "
"dictionary has height 0."
msgstr ""
"C’est le nombre de clés du chemin le plus long. Les clés de premier "
"niveau sont à la profondeur 0 ; le résultat est donc la plus grande "
"profondeur d’une clé plus 1. Un dictionnaire vide a une hauteur de 0."

msgid "Number of keys on the longest path"
msgstr "Nombre de clés du chemin le plus long"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': 1})\n"
">>> nd.height()\n"
"1"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': 1})\n"
">>> nd.height()\n"
"1"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}})\n"
">>> nd.height()\n"
"3"
msgstr ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}})\n"
">>> nd.height()\n"
"3"

msgid ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary()\n"
">>> nd.height()\n"
"0"
msgstr ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary()\n"
">>> nd.height()\n"
"0"

msgid "Empty dictionary has height 0"
msgstr "Un dictionnaire vide a une hauteur de 0"

msgid "Single-level dictionary has height 1"
msgstr "Un dictionnaire à un seul niveau a une hauteur de 1"

msgid "O(n) complexity where n is number of paths"
msgstr "Complexité O(n), où n est le nombre de chemins"

msgid ":py:obj:`size`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`size`"

msgid "Count every key"
msgstr "Compte toutes les clés"

msgid ":py:obj:`leaves`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`leaves`"

msgid "Get all leaf values"
msgstr "Renvoie toutes les valeurs des feuilles"

msgid "Check if the nested structure is height-balanced."
msgstr "Teste si la structure imbriquée est équilibrée en hauteur."

msgid ""
"A balanced dictionary is one where the height difference between any two "
"subtrees at the same level differs by at most 1. This indicates a "
"relatively uniform distribution of nesting depth."
msgstr ""
"Un dictionnaire équilibré est un dictionnaire dans lequel la différence "
"de hauteur entre deux sous-arbres quelconques d’un même niveau est d’au "
"plus 1. Cela indique une répartition relativement uniforme de la "
"profondeur d’imbrication."

msgid "True if structure is balanced, False otherwise"
msgstr "True si la structure est équilibrée, False sinon"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> # Balanced\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': {'d': 2}})\n"
">>> nd.is_balanced()\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> # Équilibré\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': {'d': 2}})\n"
">>> nd.is_balanced()\n"
"True"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # Unbalanced\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}, 'd': 2})\n"
">>> nd.is_balanced()\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> # Déséquilibré\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}, 'd': 2})\n"
">>> nd.is_balanced()\n"
"False"

msgid "Uses recursive height calculation"
msgstr "Utilise un calcul récursif de la hauteur"

msgid "Checks balance at every node"
msgstr "Vérifie l’équilibre à chaque nœud"

msgid "Empty dictionary is considered balanced"
msgstr "Un dictionnaire vide est considéré comme équilibré"

msgid "Useful for identifying skewed structures"
msgstr "Utile pour repérer les structures déséquilibrées"

msgid ":py:obj:`height`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`height`"

msgid "Get maximum depth"
msgstr "Renvoie la profondeur maximale"

msgid "Check if an atomic key exists at any level in the hierarchy."
msgstr "Teste si une clé atomique existe à un niveau quelconque de la hiérarchie."

msgid ""
"Searches through all hierarchical paths to determine if the given atomic "
"key appears anywhere in the nested structure. Does not accept "
"hierarchical paths (lists)."
msgstr ""
"Parcourt tous les chemins hiérarchiques pour déterminer si la clé "
"atomique donnée apparaît quelque part dans la structure imbriquée. "
"N’accepte pas les chemins hiérarchiques (listes)."

msgid "Atomic key to search for (not a list)"
msgstr "Clé atomique à rechercher (pas une liste)"

msgid "True if key exists at any level"
msgstr "True si la clé existe à un niveau quelconque"

msgid "If key is a list (hierarchical keys not allowed)"
msgstr "Si la clé est une liste (les clés hiérarchiques ne sont pas acceptées)"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd.is_key('b')\n"
"True\n"
">>> nd.is_key('c')\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd.is_key('b')\n"
"True\n"
">>> nd.is_key('c')\n"
"False"

msgid ""
">>> # Lists not allowed\n"
">>> nd.is_key(['a', 'b'])\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedKeyError: \"This function manages only "
"atomic keys..."
msgstr ""
">>> # Les listes ne sont pas acceptées\n"
">>> nd.is_key(['a', 'b'])\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedKeyError: \"This function manages only "
"atomic keys..."

msgid "Only searches for atomic keys"
msgstr "Ne recherche que des clés atomiques"

msgid "Checks all nesting levels"
msgstr "Examine tous les niveaux d’imbrication"

msgid "O(n) complexity where n is total number of keys"
msgstr "Complexité O(n), où n est le nombre total de clés"

msgid ":py:obj:`occurrences`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`occurrences`"

msgid "Count how many times key appears"
msgstr "Compte le nombre d’apparitions d’une clé"

msgid ":py:obj:`key_list`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`key_list`"

msgid "Get all paths containing the key"
msgstr "Renvoie tous les chemins qui contiennent la clé"

msgid "Check if two nested dictionaries are isomorphic."
msgstr "Teste si deux dictionnaires imbriqués sont isomorphes."

msgid ""
"Two structures are isomorphic if they: 1. Are both nested dictionaries "
"(any class of the family) 2. Have identical dictionary content (keys and "
"values)"
msgstr ""
"Deux structures sont isomorphes si : 1. ce sont toutes deux des "
"dictionnaires imbriqués (de n’importe quelle classe de la famille) 2. "
"elles ont le même contenu (clés et valeurs)"

msgid ""
"They describe the same nested structure, up to the choice of class: a "
"NestedDictionary and a StrictNestedDictionary with the same content "
"differ only in what reading a missing key does. Configuration differences"
" are ignored. A plain dict is never isomorphic."
msgstr ""
"Elles décrivent la même structure imbriquée, au choix de la classe près :"
" un NestedDictionary et un StrictNestedDictionary de même contenu ne "
"diffèrent que par l’effet de la lecture d’une clé absente. Les "
"différences de configuration sont ignorées. Un dict simple n’est jamais "
"isomorphe."

msgid "True if both are nested dictionaries with the same content"
msgstr "True si les deux sont des dictionnaires imbriqués de même contenu"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> from ndict_tools import StrictNestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd1 = NestedDictionary({'a': 1})\n"
">>> nd2 = StrictNestedDictionary({'a': 1})\n"
">>> nd1.equal(nd2)\n"
"False\n"
">>> nd1.isomorph(nd2)\n"
"True\n"
">>> nd1.isomorph({'a': 1})\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> from ndict_tools import StrictNestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd1 = NestedDictionary({'a': 1})\n"
">>> nd2 = StrictNestedDictionary({'a': 1})\n"
">>> nd1.equal(nd2)\n"
"False\n"
">>> nd1.isomorph(nd2)\n"
"True\n"
">>> nd1.isomorph({'a': 1})\n"
"False"

msgid ":py:obj:`equal`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`equal`"

msgid "Strict equality (includes class and setup)"
msgstr "Égalité stricte (inclut la classe et la configuration)"

msgid "Same content only, plain dicts accepted"
msgstr "Même contenu seulement, les dict simples sont acceptés"

msgid "Get all values associated with paths containing a specific key."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie toutes les valeurs associées aux chemins qui contiennent une clé "
"donnée."

msgid ""
"Returns a list of all terminal values whose hierarchical paths contain "
"the specified atomic key at any position."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie la liste de toutes les valeurs terminales dont le chemin "
"hiérarchique contient la clé atomique indiquée, à n’importe quelle "
"position."

msgid "Atomic key to search for"
msgstr "Clé atomique à rechercher"

msgid "list of values from paths containing the key"
msgstr "liste des valeurs des chemins qui contiennent la clé"

msgid "If key doesn't exist in the dictionary"
msgstr "Si la clé n’existe pas dans le dictionnaire"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': {'b': 2}})\n"
">>> nd.items_list('b')\n"
"[1, 2]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': {'b': 2}})\n"
">>> nd.items_list('b')\n"
"[1, 2]"

msgid ""
">>> nd.items_list('a')\n"
"[1]"
msgstr ""
">>> nd.items_list('a')\n"
"[1]"

msgid ""
">>> nd.items_list('nonexistent')\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedKeyError: 'Cannot find the key: "
"nonexistent..."
msgstr ""
">>> nd.items_list('nonexistent')\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedKeyError: 'Cannot find the key: "
"nonexistent..."

msgid "Returns values in the order they're encountered during traversal"
msgstr ""
"Renvoie les valeurs dans l’ordre où elles sont rencontrées pendant le "
"parcours"

msgid "Multiple values returned if key appears in multiple paths"
msgstr "Plusieurs valeurs sont renvoyées si la clé apparaît dans plusieurs chemins"

msgid "Only returns terminal (leaf) values"
msgstr "Ne renvoie que les valeurs terminales (des feuilles)"

msgid "Get paths containing the key"
msgstr "Renvoie les chemins qui contiennent la clé"

msgid "Get all hierarchical paths containing a specific key."
msgstr "Renvoie tous les chemins hiérarchiques qui contiennent une clé donnée."

msgid ""
"Returns a list of all complete paths (as tuples) that contain the "
"specified atomic key at any position in the path."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie la liste de tous les chemins complets (sous forme de tuples) qui "
"contiennent la clé atomique indiquée, à n’importe quelle position du "
"chemin."

msgid "list of paths (as tuples) containing the key"
msgstr "liste des chemins (sous forme de tuples) qui contiennent la clé"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': {'b': 2}})\n"
">>> nd.key_list('b')\n"
"[('a', 'b'), ('c', 'b')]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': {'b': 2}})\n"
">>> nd.key_list('b')\n"
"[('a', 'b'), ('c', 'b')]"

msgid ""
">>> nd.key_list('a')\n"
"[('a', 'b')]"
msgstr ""
">>> nd.key_list('a')\n"
"[('a', 'b')]"

msgid ""
">>> nd.key_list('nonexistent')\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedKeyError: 'Cannot find the key: "
"nonexistent..."
msgstr ""
">>> nd.key_list('nonexistent')\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedKeyError: 'Cannot find the key: "
"nonexistent..."

msgid ":py:obj:`is_key`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`is_key`"

msgid "Check if key exists"
msgstr "Teste si la clé existe"

msgid ":py:obj:`items_list`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`items_list`"

msgid "Get values at paths containing key"
msgstr "Renvoie les valeurs des chemins qui contiennent la clé"

msgid "Count occurrences"
msgstr "Compte les occurrences"

msgid "Extract the values of all leaf keys from the nested structure."
msgstr "Extrait les valeurs de toutes les clés feuilles de la structure imbriquée."

msgid ""
"A leaf is a key without children: its value is either not a nested "
"dictionary, or an empty one. Returns the values of these keys."
msgstr ""
"Une feuille est une clé sans enfant : sa valeur n’est pas un dictionnaire"
" imbriqué, ou en est un vide. Renvoie les valeurs de ces clés."

msgid "list of all leaf values"
msgstr "liste de toutes les valeurs des feuilles"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> nd.leaves()\n"
"[1, 2]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> nd.leaves()\n"
"[1, 2]"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}})\n"
">>> nd.leaves()\n"
"[1]"
msgstr ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}})\n"
">>> nd.leaves()\n"
"[1]"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # Empty dict as leaf value\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {}})\n"
">>> [type(value).__name__ for value in nd.leaves()]\n"
"['NestedDictionary']"
msgstr ""
">>> # Un dict vide comme valeur de feuille\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {}})\n"
">>> [type(value).__name__ for value in nd.leaves()]\n"
"['NestedDictionary']"

msgid "Returns values in DFS order"
msgstr "Renvoie les valeurs dans l’ordre du parcours en profondeur"

msgid "Empty dictionaries are considered leaf values"
msgstr "Les dictionnaires vides sont considérés comme des valeurs de feuilles"

msgid "Plain dicts (not nested dictionaries of the family) are also leaves"
msgstr ""
"Les dict simples (qui ne sont pas des dictionnaires imbriqués de la "
"famille) sont aussi des feuilles"

msgid ":py:obj:`unpacked_values`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`unpacked_values`"

msgid "Generator alternative"
msgstr "Alternative sous forme de générateur"

msgid "Traversal including intermediate nodes"
msgstr "Parcours incluant les nœuds intermédiaires"

msgid "Count occurrences of an atomic key throughout the hierarchy."
msgstr "Compte les occurrences d’une clé atomique dans toute la hiérarchie."

msgid ""
"Returns the total number of times a key appears in the nested structure, "
"counting each occurrence in every hierarchical path."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie le nombre total d’apparitions d’une clé dans la structure "
"imbriquée, en comptant chaque occurrence dans chaque chemin hiérarchique."

msgid "Atomic key to count"
msgstr "Clé atomique à compter"

msgid "Number of occurrences (0 if key doesn't exist)"
msgstr "Nombre d’occurrences (0 si la clé n’existe pas)"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': {'b': 2}})\n"
">>> nd.occurrences('b')\n"
"2\n"
">>> nd.occurrences('a')\n"
"1\n"
">>> nd.occurrences('z')\n"
"0"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': {'b': 2}})\n"
">>> nd.occurrences('b')\n"
"2\n"
">>> nd.occurrences('a')\n"
"1\n"
">>> nd.occurrences('z')\n"
"0"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # Key appearing multiple times in same path\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'a': 1}})\n"
">>> nd.occurrences('a')\n"
"2"
msgstr ""
">>> # Clé qui apparaît plusieurs fois dans un même chemin\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'a': 1}})\n"
">>> nd.occurrences('a')\n"
"2"

msgid "Remove and return value at key or hierarchical path."
msgstr "Supprime et renvoie la valeur d’une clé ou d’un chemin hiérarchique."

msgid ""
"Removes the specified key (flat or hierarchical) and returns its value. "
"Automatically cleans up empty parent dictionaries after removal. If the "
"key doesn't exist, returns the default value, ``None`` included, or "
"raises an error when no default is given, as ``dict.pop`` does."
msgstr ""
"Supprime la clé indiquée (simple ou hiérarchique) et renvoie sa valeur. "
"Supprime automatiquement les dictionnaires parents vidés par la "
"suppression. Si la clé n’existe pas, renvoie la valeur par défaut, "
"``None`` compris, ou lève une erreur lorsqu’aucune valeur par défaut "
"n’est fournie, comme le fait ``dict.pop``."

msgid "Single key or hierarchical path to remove"
msgstr "Clé simple ou chemin hiérarchique à supprimer"

msgid "Value to return if key doesn't exist"
msgstr "Valeur à renvoyer si la clé n’existe pas"

msgid "The value that was removed"
msgstr "La valeur supprimée"

msgid "If key doesn't exist and no default provided"
msgstr "Si la clé n’existe pas et qu’aucune valeur par défaut n’est fournie"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> nd.pop('c')\n"
"2\n"
">>> 'c' in nd\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> nd.pop('c')\n"
"2\n"
">>> 'c' in nd\n"
"False"

msgid ""
">>> # Hierarchical key\n"
">>> nd.pop(['a', 'b'])\n"
"1\n"
">>> 'a' in nd  # Empty 'a' was removed\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> # Clé hiérarchique\n"
">>> nd.pop(['a', 'b'])\n"
"1\n"
">>> 'a' in nd  # 'a', vidé, a été supprimé\n"
"False"

msgid ""
">>> # With default\n"
">>> nd.pop('nonexistent', 'default_value')\n"
"'default_value'\n"
">>> nd.pop('nonexistent', None) is None  # None is a valid default\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> # Avec une valeur par défaut\n"
">>> nd.pop('nonexistent', 'default_value')\n"
"'default_value'\n"
">>> nd.pop('nonexistent', None) is None  # None est une valeur par défaut"
" valide\n"
"True"

msgid ":py:obj:`popitem`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`popitem`"

msgid "Remove and return last item"
msgstr "Supprime et renvoie le dernier élément"

msgid ":py:obj:`__delitem__`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`__delitem__`"

msgid "Delete without returning value"
msgstr "Supprime sans renvoyer la valeur"

msgid "Remove and return the last item as (path, value) pair."
msgstr ""
"Supprime et renvoie le dernier élément sous forme de paire (chemin, "
"valeur)."

msgid ""
"Removes the last item in the most deeply nested dictionary, returning its"
" full hierarchical path and value. Uses depth-first traversal to locate "
"the deepest rightmost item."
msgstr ""
"Supprime le dernier élément du dictionnaire le plus profondément imbriqué"
" et renvoie son chemin hiérarchique complet et sa valeur. Utilise un "
"parcours en profondeur pour trouver l’élément le plus profond et le plus "
"à droite."

msgid "(path_list, value) where path_list is the hierarchical path"
msgstr "(path_list, valeur), où path_list est le chemin hiérarchique"

msgid "If the dictionary is empty"
msgstr "Si le dictionnaire est vide"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}})\n"
">>> path, value = nd.popitem()\n"
">>> path\n"
"['a', 'c']\n"
">>> value\n"
"2"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}})\n"
">>> path, value = nd.popitem()\n"
">>> path\n"
"['a', 'c']\n"
">>> value\n"
"2"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> nd.popitem()\n"
"(['a', 'b'], 1)\n"
">>> nd.to_dict()  # The emptied parent 'a' stays\n"
"{'a': {}}"
msgstr ""
">>> nd.popitem()\n"
"(['a', 'b'], 1)\n"
">>> nd.to_dict()  # Le parent 'a', vidé, est conservé\n"
"{'a': {}}"

msgid ""
">>> # Empty dictionary\n"
">>> NestedDictionary().popitem()\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedIndexError: popitem(): NestedDictionary is "
"empty"
msgstr ""
">>> # Dictionnaire vide\n"
">>> NestedDictionary().popitem()\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"ndict_tools.exception.StackedIndexError: popitem(): NestedDictionary is "
"empty"

msgid "Follows DFS to find the last (rightmost, deepest) item"
msgstr ""
"Suit le parcours en profondeur pour trouver le dernier élément (le plus à"
" droite, le plus profond)"

msgid ""
"Removes one key at a time: a parent emptied by the removal stays in "
"place, unlike ``del`` and ``pop()``"
msgstr ""
"Supprime une clé à la fois : un parent vidé par la suppression reste en "
"place, contrairement à ``del`` et ``pop()``"

msgid "Path is returned as a list of keys"
msgstr "Le chemin est renvoyé sous forme de liste de clés"

msgid ":py:obj:`pop`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`pop`"

msgid "Remove item by key"
msgstr "Supprime un élément par sa clé"

msgid "View all (path, value) pairs"
msgstr "Vue de toutes les paires (chemin, valeur)"

msgid "Check if two structures have the same content, whatever holds it."
msgstr ""
"Teste si deux structures ont le même contenu, quel que soit ce qui le "
"contient."

msgid ""
"Two structures are similar if they represent the same nested dictionary "
"content, regardless of whether they are nested dictionaries of the family"
" or plain dicts. Class and configuration are ignored."
msgstr ""
"Deux structures sont similaires si elles représentent le même contenu de "
"dictionnaire imbriqué, qu’il s’agisse de dictionnaires imbriqués de la "
"famille ou de dict simples. La classe et la configuration sont ignorées."

msgid "Dictionary to compare with"
msgstr "Dictionnaire à comparer"

msgid "True if ``other`` is a dict with the same content"
msgstr "True si ``other`` est un dict de même contenu"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd.similar({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
"True\n"
">>> nd.similar({'a': {'b': 2}})\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd.similar({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
"True\n"
">>> nd.similar({'a': {'b': 2}})\n"
"False"

msgid ""
"Checks if self[k1]...[kn] == other[k1]...[kn] for all paths. This is the "
"most permissive comparison method: ``equal`` implies ``isomorph``, which "
"implies ``similar``."
msgstr ""
"Vérifie que self[k1]...[kn] == other[k1]...[kn] pour tous les chemins. "
"C’est la méthode de comparaison la plus permissive : ``equal`` implique "
"``isomorph``, qui implique ``similar``."

msgid "Strict equality"
msgstr "Égalité stricte"

msgid "Compute the total number of keys (nodes) in the structure."
msgstr "Calcule le nombre total de clés (nœuds) de la structure."

msgid ""
"Counts all keys at all nesting levels, including both intermediate "
"dictionary keys and terminal value keys."
msgstr ""
"Compte toutes les clés à tous les niveaux d’imbrication, aussi bien les "
"clés de dictionnaires intermédiaires que les clés de valeurs terminales."

msgid "Total number of keys across all levels"
msgstr "Nombre total de clés sur tous les niveaux"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd.size()\n"
"2"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd.size()\n"
"2"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> nd.size()\n"
"4"
msgstr ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> nd.size()\n"
"4"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # A key whose value is an empty dictionary counts\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {}})\n"
">>> nd.size()\n"
"1"
msgstr ""
">>> # Une clé dont la valeur est un dictionnaire vide compte\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {}})\n"
">>> nd.size()\n"
"1"

msgid "Counts all keys at all levels"
msgstr "Compte toutes les clés à tous les niveaux"

msgid "Equivalent to number of nodes in tree representation"
msgstr "Équivaut au nombre de nœuds de la représentation en arbre"

msgid "Different from len() which only counts top-level keys"
msgstr "Diffère de len(), qui ne compte que les clés de premier niveau"

msgid "Get the number of levels"
msgstr "Renvoie le nombre de niveaux"

msgid ":py:obj:`__len__`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`__len__`"

msgid "Get top-level key count"
msgstr "Renvoie le nombre de clés de premier niveau"

msgid "Convert to a standard nested dictionary."
msgstr "Convertit en dictionnaire imbriqué standard."

msgid ""
"Recursively converts the nested dictionary and all its nested levels to "
"regular Python dictionaries, removing all special functionality but "
"preserving the structure."
msgstr ""
"Convertit récursivement le dictionnaire imbriqué et tous ses niveaux en "
"dictionnaires Python ordinaires, en supprimant toutes les fonctionnalités"
" particulières mais en conservant la structure."

msgid "Regular nested dictionary with same structure"
msgstr "Dictionnaire imbriqué ordinaire de même structure"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> regular = nd.to_dict()\n"
">>> type(regular)\n"
"<class 'dict'>\n"
">>> regular\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}}"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> regular = nd.to_dict()\n"
">>> type(regular)\n"
"<class 'dict'>\n"
">>> regular\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}}"

msgid "All nested levels are converted recursively"
msgstr "Tous les niveaux imbriqués sont convertis récursivement"

msgid "Other value types are preserved as-is"
msgstr "Les autres types de valeurs sont conservés tels quels"

msgid "Inverse operation of from_dict()"
msgstr "Opération inverse de from_dict()"

msgid ":py:obj:`from_dict`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`from_dict`"

msgid "Convert a dict to a nested dictionary"
msgstr "Convertit un dict en dictionnaire imbriqué"

msgid "Create a deep copy"
msgstr "Crée une copie profonde"

msgid "Serialize this dictionary to a JSON file."
msgstr "Sérialise ce dictionnaire dans un fichier JSON."

msgid ""
"Non-string keys are written in square brackets (e.g., integer key ``42`` "
"→ ``\"[42]\"``, tuple key ``(1, 2)`` → ``\"[(1, 2)]\"``); a string key "
"that starts with ``[`` is escaped with a backslash. Round-trips are "
"lossless for supported types: ``str``, ``int``, ``float``, ``bool``, flat"
" ``tuple``, flat ``frozenset``. File I/O is delegated to ``json.dump``."
msgstr ""
"Les clés qui ne sont pas des chaînes sont écrites entre crochets (par "
"exemple la clé entière ``42`` → ``\"[42]\"``, la clé tuple ``(1, 2)`` → "
"``\"[(1, 2)]\"``) ; une clé chaîne qui commence par ``[`` est échappée "
"par une barre oblique inverse. L’aller-retour est sans perte pour les "
"types pris en charge : ``str``, ``int``, ``float``, ``bool``, ``tuple`` "
"plat, ``frozenset`` plat. Les entrées-sorties de fichier sont déléguées à"
" ``json.dump``."

msgid "Destination file path."
msgstr "Chemin du fichier de destination."

msgid "JSON indentation level. Defaults to ``self.indent`` if not provided."
msgstr "Niveau d’indentation JSON. Vaut ``self.indent`` s’il n’est pas fourni."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> import tempfile\n"
">>> from pathlib import Path\n"
">>> tmp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n"
">>> path = Path(tmp.name) / 'nd.json'\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd.to_json(path)\n"
">>> path.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\n"
"'{\"a\": {\"b\": 1}}'\n"
">>> tmp.cleanup()"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> import tempfile\n"
">>> from pathlib import Path\n"
">>> tmp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n"
">>> path = Path(tmp.name) / 'nd.json'\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> nd.to_json(path)\n"
">>> path.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\n"
"'{\"a\": {\"b\": 1}}'\n"
">>> tmp.cleanup()"

msgid ":py:obj:`from_json`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`from_json`"

msgid "Reconstruct from a JSON file."
msgstr "Reconstruit à partir d’un fichier JSON."

msgid "Serialize this dictionary to a pickle file with SHA-256 verification."
msgstr ""
"Sérialise ce dictionnaire dans un fichier pickle, avec vérification "
"SHA-256."

msgid "Writes two files: ``<path>`` (pickle) and ``<path>.sha256`` (hex digest)."
msgstr ""
"Écrit deux fichiers : ``<path>`` (pickle) et ``<path>.sha256`` (empreinte"
" hexadécimale)."

msgid "Pickle protocol. Defaults to ``pickle.DEFAULT_PROTOCOL``."
msgstr "Protocole pickle. Vaut ``pickle.DEFAULT_PROTOCOL`` par défaut."

msgid ":py:obj:`from_pickle`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`from_pickle`"

msgid "Reconstruct from a pickle file."
msgstr "Reconstruit à partir d’un fichier pickle."

msgid "Generate all (path, value) pairs from nested structure."
msgstr "Produit toutes les paires (chemin, valeur) de la structure imbriquée."

msgid ""
"Yields terminal values along with their hierarchical paths as tuples. "
"This provides a flattened view of the entire nested dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Produit les valeurs terminales avec leur chemin hiérarchique sous forme "
"de tuple. Cela donne une vue aplatie de l’ensemble du dictionnaire "
"imbriqué."

msgid "*tuple* -- (path_tuple, value) for each terminal value"
msgstr "*tuple* -- (path_tuple, valeur) pour chaque valeur terminale"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> list(nd.unpacked_items())\n"
"[(('a', 'b'), 1), (('c',), 2)]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> list(nd.unpacked_items())\n"
"[(('a', 'b'), 1), (('c',), 2)]"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # Empty dict as value\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {}})\n"
">>> [(path, type(value).__name__) for path, value in nd.unpacked_items()]"
"\n"
"[(('a',), 'NestedDictionary')]"
msgstr ""
">>> # Un dict vide comme valeur\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {}})\n"
">>> [(path, type(value).__name__) for path, value in nd.unpacked_items()]"
"\n"
"[(('a',), 'NestedDictionary')]"

msgid "Uses depth-first traversal"
msgstr "Utilise un parcours en profondeur"

msgid "Empty dictionaries are treated as terminal values"
msgstr "Les dictionnaires vides sont traités comme des valeurs terminales"

msgid "Paths are immutable tuples for hashability"
msgstr "Les chemins sont des tuples immuables, donc hachables"

msgid ":py:obj:`unpacked_keys`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`unpacked_keys`"

msgid "Get only the paths"
msgstr "Renvoie seulement les chemins"

msgid "Get only the values"
msgstr "Renvoie seulement les valeurs"

msgid "Depth-first traversal alternative returning lists"
msgstr "Alternative par parcours en profondeur, qui renvoie des listes"

msgid "Generate all hierarchical paths (keys) from nested structure."
msgstr "Produit tous les chemins hiérarchiques (clés) de la structure imbriquée."

msgid ""
"Yields the path to each terminal value as a tuple of keys, providing "
"access to all navigable paths in the dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Produit le chemin de chaque valeur terminale sous forme de tuple de clés,"
" ce qui donne accès à tous les chemins navigables du dictionnaire."

msgid "*tuple* -- Path as tuple of keys"
msgstr "*tuple* -- Chemin sous forme de tuple de clés"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> list(nd.unpacked_keys())\n"
"[('a', 'b')]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> list(nd.unpacked_keys())\n"
"[('a', 'b')]"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> sorted(nd.unpacked_keys())\n"
"[('a', 'b'), ('a', 'c'), ('d',)]"
msgstr ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> sorted(nd.unpacked_keys())\n"
"[('a', 'b'), ('a', 'c'), ('d',)]"

msgid "Get (path, value) pairs"
msgstr "Renvoie les paires (chemin, valeur)"

msgid "Get the paths as a view object"
msgstr "Renvoie les chemins sous forme d’objet vue"

msgid "Generate all terminal values from nested structure."
msgstr "Produit toutes les valeurs terminales de la structure imbriquée."

msgid ""
"Yields only the leaf values, discarding path information. Useful for "
"collecting all data values regardless of structure."
msgstr ""
"Ne produit que les valeurs des feuilles, sans l’information de chemin. "
"Utile pour recueillir toutes les valeurs de données, quelle que soit la "
"structure."

msgid "*Any* -- Each leaf value in the nested dictionary"
msgstr "*Any* -- Chaque valeur de feuille du dictionnaire imbriqué"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> list(nd.unpacked_values())\n"
"[1, 2]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> list(nd.unpacked_values())\n"
"[1, 2]"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # Empty dict is a value\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {}, 'b': 1})\n"
">>> [type(value).__name__ for value in nd.unpacked_values()]\n"
"['NestedDictionary', 'int']"
msgstr ""
">>> # Un dict vide est une valeur\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {}, 'b': 1})\n"
">>> [type(value).__name__ for value in nd.unpacked_values()]\n"
"['NestedDictionary', 'int']"

msgid "Alternative method returning list"
msgstr "Méthode alternative qui renvoie une liste"

msgid ""
"Update the nested dictionary with key/value pairs from mapping, iterable,"
" or kwargs."
msgstr ""
"Met à jour le dictionnaire imbriqué avec les paires clé/valeur d’un "
"mapping, d’un itérable ou d’arguments nommés."

msgid ""
"Merges the provided mapping, iterable of key-value pairs, or keyword "
"arguments into this nested dictionary, converting regular dicts to nested"
" levels recursively while preserving the nested dictionaries already "
"given. Those keep their identity and receive this instance's "
"configuration through the ``default_setup`` setter."
msgstr ""
"Fusionne dans ce dictionnaire imbriqué le mapping, l’itérable de paires "
"clé-valeur ou les arguments nommés fournis, en convertissant "
"récursivement les dict ordinaires en niveaux imbriqués et en conservant "
"les dictionnaires imbriqués déjà fournis. Ceux-ci gardent leur identité "
"et reçoivent la configuration de cette instance par le setter "
"``default_setup``."

msgid ""
"Positional-only. A mapping (dict, nested dictionary), any object with "
"``keys()`` and ``__getitem__``, or an iterable of (key, value) tuples to "
"merge, as accepted by ``dict.update``. If None, only kwargs are used."
msgstr ""
"Positionnel uniquement. Un mapping (dict, dictionnaire imbriqué), tout "
"objet doté de ``keys()`` et de ``__getitem__``, ou un itérable de tuples "
"(clé, valeur) à fusionner, tel qu’accepté par ``dict.update``. Si None, "
"seuls les arguments nommés sont utilisés."

msgid "Additional key/value pairs to merge"
msgstr "Paires clé/valeur supplémentaires à fusionner"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': 1})"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': 1})"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # From dict\n"
">>> nd.update({'b': 2, 'c': {'d': 3}})\n"
">>> nd['c']['d']\n"
"3"
msgstr ""
">>> # À partir d’un dict\n"
">>> nd.update({'b': 2, 'c': {'d': 3}})\n"
">>> nd['c']['d']\n"
"3"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # From iterable\n"
">>> nd.update([('e', 4), ('f', {'g': 5})])\n"
">>> nd['f']['g']\n"
"5"
msgstr ""
">>> # À partir d’un itérable\n"
">>> nd.update([('e', 4), ('f', {'g': 5})])\n"
">>> nd['f']['g']\n"
"5"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # Using kwargs\n"
">>> nd.update(h=6, i={'j': 7})\n"
">>> nd['i']['j']\n"
"7"
msgstr ""
">>> # Avec des arguments nommés\n"
">>> nd.update(h=6, i={'j': 7})\n"
">>> nd['i']['j']\n"
"7"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> # Combined\n"
">>> nd.update({'k': 8}, l=9)\n"
">>> nd['k'], nd['l']\n"
"(8, 9)"
msgstr ""
">>> # Les deux à la fois\n"
">>> nd.update({'k': 8}, l=9)\n"
">>> nd['k'], nd['l']\n"
"(8, 9)"

msgid ""
"Accepts mappings (dict, nested dictionary, etc.) and any object with "
"``keys()`` and ``__getitem__``"
msgstr ""
"Accepte les mappings (dict, dictionnaire imbriqué, etc.) et tout objet "
"doté de ``keys()`` et de ``__getitem__``"

msgid "Accepts iterables of (key, value) tuples"
msgstr "Accepte les itérables de tuples (clé, valeur)"

msgid "Accepts keyword arguments"
msgstr "Accepte les arguments nommés"

msgid "Regular dicts are converted to nested levels recursively"
msgstr "Les dict ordinaires sont convertis récursivement en niveaux imbriqués"

msgid "Nested dictionaries are accepted directly with synchronized config"
msgstr ""
"Les dictionnaires imbriqués sont acceptés directement, avec une "
"configuration synchronisée"

msgid "Configuration is synchronized across all nested instances"
msgstr "La configuration est synchronisée entre toutes les instances imbriquées"

msgid "Later values override earlier ones for duplicate keys"
msgstr ""
"Pour les clés en double, les valeurs ultérieures remplacent les "
"précédentes"

msgid ":py:obj:`__init__`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`__init__`"

msgid "Initialization with data"
msgstr "Initialisation avec des données"

msgid ":py:obj:`__setitem__`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`__setitem__`"

msgid "set individual items"
msgstr "définit des éléments individuels"

msgid "indent is used to print the dictionary with json indentation"
msgstr "indent sert à afficher le dictionnaire avec une indentation de type JSON"

msgid "Strict nested dictionary class."
msgstr "Classe de dictionnaire imbriqué strict."

msgid ""
"This class is designed to implement a non-default answer to an unknown "
"key."
msgstr ""
"Cette classe est conçue pour donner une réponse autre que la réponse par "
"défaut à une clé inconnue."

msgid "Initial data, as for ``NestedDictionary``"
msgstr "Données initiales, comme pour ``NestedDictionary``"

msgid ""
"Configuration (keyword-only). Its ``default_factory`` is overridden; "
"``indent`` defaults to 0. The mapping is not modified."
msgstr ""
"Configuration (argument nommé uniquement). Son ``default_factory`` est "
"imposé ; ``indent`` vaut 0 par défaut. Le mapping n’est pas modifié."

msgid "Initial data given as keyword arguments"
msgstr "Données initiales fournies comme arguments nommés"

msgid ""
"This class overwrites the default_factory attribute to None, preventing "
"automatic creation of nested dictionaries for unknown keys."
msgstr ""
"Cette classe fixe l’attribut default_factory à None, ce qui empêche la "
"création automatique de dictionnaires imbriqués pour les clés inconnues."

msgid ""
"All methods are inherited from :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`. "
"The only difference is the behaviour on unknown keys: a :class:`KeyError`"
" is raised instead of silently creating a new nested dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Toutes les méthodes sont héritées de "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`. La seule différence est le "
"comportement sur les clés inconnues : une :class:`KeyError` est levée au "
"lieu de créer silencieusement un nouveau dictionnaire imbriqué."

msgid "Smooth nested dictionary class."
msgstr "Classe de dictionnaire imbriqué souple."

msgid ""
"This class is designed to implement a default answer as an empty "
"SmoothNestedDictionary to an unknown key."
msgstr ""
"Cette classe est conçue pour répondre à une clé inconnue par un "
"SmoothNestedDictionary vide."

msgid ""
"This class overwrites the default_factory attribute to "
"SmoothNestedDictionary, automatically creating nested dictionaries for "
"unknown keys."
msgstr ""
"Cette classe fixe l’attribut default_factory à SmoothNestedDictionary, ce"
" qui crée automatiquement des dictionnaires imbriqués pour les clés "
"inconnues."

msgid ""
"All methods are inherited from :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`. "
"The only difference is that every access to an unknown key returns a new "
"empty :class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary` — even at arbitrary "
"depth."
msgstr ""
"Toutes les méthodes sont héritées de "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`. La seule différence est que tout "
"accès à une clé inconnue renvoie un nouveau "
":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary` vide, même à une profondeur "
"quelconque."

msgid "Path views"
msgstr "Vues des chemins"

msgid "A view providing access to all hierarchical paths in a nested dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Une vue qui donne accès à tous les chemins hiérarchiques d’un "
"dictionnaire imbriqué."

msgid ""
"Similar to the standard ``dict.keys()`` view, but designed specifically "
"for hierarchical paths in nested dictionaries. Provides lazy iteration "
"over all paths without storing them in memory."
msgstr ""
"Semblable à la vue standard ``dict.keys()``, mais conçu spécialement pour"
" les chemins hiérarchiques des dictionnaires imbriqués. Permet une "
"itération paresseuse sur tous les chemins sans les stocker en mémoire."

msgid ""
"This is the public API for working with paths: its conversions return "
"public class instances."
msgstr ""
"C’est l’API publique pour travailler avec les chemins : ses conversions "
"renvoient des instances de classes publiques."

msgid ""
"The nested dictionary to create a view for (any class of the "
"NestedDictionary family)"
msgstr ""
"Le dictionnaire imbriqué dont on crée une vue (de n’importe quelle classe"
" de la famille NestedDictionary)"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> paths = nd.paths()\n"
">>> type(paths).__name__\n"
"'PathsView'"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> paths = nd.paths()\n"
">>> type(paths).__name__\n"
"'PathsView'"

msgid ""
">>> # Iterate over paths\n"
">>> for path in paths:\n"
"...     print(path)\n"
"['a']\n"
"['a', 'b']\n"
"['a', 'c']\n"
"['d']"
msgstr ""
">>> # Parcourt les chemins\n"
">>> for path in paths:\n"
"...     print(path)\n"
"['a']\n"
"['a', 'b']\n"
"['a', 'c']\n"
"['d']"

msgid ""
">>> # Get leaf paths only\n"
">>> paths.get_leaf_paths()\n"
"[['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"
msgstr ""
">>> # Chemins des feuilles seulement\n"
">>> paths.get_leaf_paths()\n"
"[['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"

msgid ""
">>> # Convert to compact representation\n"
">>> compact = paths.to_compact()\n"
">>> type(compact).__name__\n"
"'CompactPathsView'"
msgstr ""
">>> # Conversion en représentation compacte\n"
">>> compact = paths.to_compact()\n"
">>> type(compact).__name__\n"
"'CompactPathsView'"

msgid "Compact representation of paths"
msgstr "Représentation compacte des chemins"

msgid ":py:obj:`NestedDictionary`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`NestedDictionary`"

msgid "Nested dictionary with path operations"
msgstr "Dictionnaire imbriqué doté d’opérations sur les chemins"

msgid "Convert this PathsView to a CompactPathsView."
msgstr "Convertit ce PathsView en CompactPathsView."

msgid "Compact representation with the same paths"
msgstr "Représentation compacte avec les mêmes chemins"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> paths = nd.paths()\n"
">>> compact = paths.to_compact()\n"
">>> compact.structure\n"
"[['a', 'b', 'c'], 'd']"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> paths = nd.paths()\n"
">>> compact = paths.to_compact()\n"
">>> compact.structure\n"
"[['a', 'b', 'c'], 'd']"

msgid "Filter paths based on a predicate function."
msgstr "Filtre les chemins selon une fonction prédicat."

msgid "Function that returns True for paths to include"
msgstr "Fonction qui renvoie True pour les chemins à inclure"

msgid "Filtered list of paths"
msgstr "Liste filtrée des chemins"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2}).paths()\n"
">>> # Get paths longer than 1\n"
">>> paths.filter_paths(lambda p: len(p) > 1)\n"
"[['a', 'b']]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2}).paths()\n"
">>> # Chemins de longueur supérieure à 1\n"
">>> paths.filter_paths(lambda p: len(p) > 1)\n"
"[['a', 'b']]"

msgid ":py:obj:`get_subtree_paths`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`get_subtree_paths`"

msgid "Filter by prefix"
msgstr "Filtre par préfixe"

msgid "Get child keys at the next level after the given path."
msgstr "Renvoie les clés enfants du niveau suivant le chemin donné."

msgid "Path to query"
msgstr "Chemin à interroger"

msgid "list of child keys, empty if path not found"
msgstr "liste des clés enfants, vide si le chemin est introuvable"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}}).paths()\n"
">>> paths.get_children(['a'])\n"
"['b', 'c']\n"
">>> paths.get_children(['a', 'b'])\n"
"[]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}}).paths()\n"
">>> paths.get_children(['a'])\n"
"['b', 'c']\n"
">>> paths.get_children(['a', 'b'])\n"
"[]"

msgid ":py:obj:`has_children`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`has_children`"

msgid "Check if path has children"
msgstr "Teste si un chemin a des enfants"

msgid "Get the number of levels of the paths."
msgstr "Renvoie le nombre de niveaux des chemins."

msgid ""
"This is the number of keys on the longest path, that is the greatest "
"depth of a key plus 1, since top-level keys have depth 0."
msgstr ""
"C’est le nombre de clés du chemin le plus long, c’est-à-dire la plus "
"grande profondeur d’une clé plus 1, puisque les clés de premier niveau "
"sont à la profondeur 0."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}}).paths()\n"
">>> paths.get_depth()\n"
"3"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}}}).paths()\n"
">>> paths.get_depth()\n"
"3"

msgid "Get all leaf paths (paths with no children)."
msgstr "Renvoie tous les chemins des feuilles (chemins sans enfant)."

msgid "list of leaf paths"
msgstr "liste des chemins des feuilles"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2}).paths()\n"
">>> paths.get_leaf_paths()\n"
"[['a', 'b'], ['c']]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2}).paths()\n"
">>> paths.get_leaf_paths()\n"
"[['a', 'b'], ['c']]"

msgid "Get all paths that start with the given prefix."
msgstr "Renvoie tous les chemins qui commencent par le préfixe donné."

msgid "Prefix to filter by"
msgstr "Préfixe de filtrage"

msgid "list of paths with this prefix"
msgstr "liste des chemins qui ont ce préfixe"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}, 'd': 2}}).paths()\n"
">>> paths.get_subtree_paths(['a'])\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'b', 'c'], ['a', 'd']]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': {'c': 1}, 'd': 2}}).paths()\n"
">>> paths.get_subtree_paths(['a'])\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'b', 'c'], ['a', 'd']]"

msgid ":py:obj:`filter_paths`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`filter_paths`"

msgid "Filter paths by predicate"
msgstr "Filtre les chemins selon un prédicat"

msgid "Check if a path has any children."
msgstr "Teste si un chemin a des enfants."

msgid "Path to check"
msgstr "Chemin à tester"

msgid "True if path has children"
msgstr "True si le chemin a des enfants"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}}).paths()\n"
">>> paths.has_children(['a'])\n"
"True\n"
">>> paths.has_children(['a', 'b'])\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}}).paths()\n"
">>> paths.has_children(['a'])\n"
"True\n"
">>> paths.has_children(['a', 'b'])\n"
"False"

msgid "A view providing compact representation of hierarchical paths."
msgstr "Une vue qui donne une représentation compacte des chemins hiérarchiques."

msgid ""
"Provides a factorized/compact representation where the hierarchical "
"structure is represented as nested lists. This is useful for efficiently "
"representing and manipulating path structures, especially when dealing "
"with large numbers of similar paths."
msgstr ""
"Fournit une représentation factorisée, ou compacte, dans laquelle la "
"structure hiérarchique est représentée par des listes imbriquées. C’est "
"utile pour représenter et manipuler efficacement des structures de "
"chemins, en particulier lorsqu’il y a beaucoup de chemins semblables."

msgid "The compact structure uses nested lists where:"
msgstr "La structure compacte utilise des listes imbriquées où :"

msgid "Leaf nodes are represented by their key alone"
msgstr "Les nœuds feuilles sont représentés par leur seule clé"

msgid "Internal nodes are represented as [key, child1, child2, ...]"
msgstr "Les nœuds internes sont représentés par [clé, enfant1, enfant2, ...]"

msgid ""
"A structure built from a dictionary is the canonical form of its paths, "
"and conversion works in both directions."
msgstr ""
"Une structure construite à partir d’un dictionnaire est la forme "
"canonique de ses chemins, et la conversion fonctionne dans les deux sens."

msgid ""
"The nested dictionary to create a compact view for (any class of the "
"NestedDictionary family)"
msgstr ""
"Le dictionnaire imbriqué dont on crée une vue compacte (de n’importe "
"quelle classe de la famille NestedDictionary)"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary, PathsView\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> cpaths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> type(cpaths).__name__\n"
"'CompactPathsView'"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary, PathsView\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> cpaths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> type(cpaths).__name__\n"
"'CompactPathsView'"

msgid ""
">>> # Get compact structure\n"
">>> cpaths.structure\n"
"[['a', 'b', 'c'], 'd']"
msgstr ""
">>> # Structure compacte\n"
">>> cpaths.structure\n"
"[['a', 'b', 'c'], 'd']"

msgid ""
">>> # Iterate over the expanded paths, as with PathsView\n"
">>> list(cpaths)\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"
msgstr ""
">>> # Parcourt les chemins développés, comme avec un PathsView\n"
">>> list(cpaths)\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"

msgid ""
">>> # Set custom structure\n"
">>> cpaths.structure = [['x', 'y', 'z']]\n"
">>> cpaths.expand()\n"
"[['x'], ['x', 'y'], ['x', 'z']]"
msgstr ""
">>> # Affecte une structure personnalisée\n"
">>> cpaths.structure = [['x', 'y', 'z']]\n"
">>> cpaths.expand()\n"
"[['x'], ['x', 'y'], ['x', 'z']]"

msgid ""
">>> # Check coverage against original dictionary\n"
">>> cpaths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> cpaths.is_covering(nd)\n"
"True\n"
">>> cpaths.coverage(nd)\n"
"1.0"
msgstr ""
">>> # Vérifie la couverture du dictionnaire d’origine\n"
">>> cpaths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> cpaths.is_covering(nd)\n"
"True\n"
">>> cpaths.coverage(nd)\n"
"1.0"

msgid ""
">>> # Partial structure\n"
">>> cpaths.structure = [['a', 'b']]\n"
">>> cpaths.coverage(nd)\n"
"0.5\n"
">>> cpaths.uncovered_paths(nd)\n"
"[['a', 'c'], ['d']]"
msgstr ""
">>> # Structure partielle\n"
">>> cpaths.structure = [['a', 'b']]\n"
">>> cpaths.coverage(nd)\n"
"0.5\n"
">>> cpaths.uncovered_paths(nd)\n"
"[['a', 'c'], ['d']]"

msgid "**Compact structure format:**"
msgstr "**Format de la structure compacte :**"

msgid "Simple leaf: ``'key'``"
msgstr "Feuille simple : ``'key'``"

msgid "Node with children: ``['key', child1, child2, ...]``"
msgstr "Nœud avec enfants : ``['key', child1, child2, ...]``"

msgid "**Examples of compact structures:**"
msgstr "**Exemples de structures compactes :**"

msgid "``[['a'], ['b']]`` → two independent paths: ``['a']`` and ``['b']``"
msgstr "``[['a'], ['b']]`` → deux chemins indépendants : ``['a']`` et ``['b']``"

msgid "``[['a', 'b', 'c']]`` → paths: ``['a']``, ``['a', 'b']``, ``['a', 'c']``"
msgstr ""
"``[['a', 'b', 'c']]`` → chemins : ``['a']``, ``['a', 'b']``, ``['a', "
"'c']``"

msgid ""
"``[['a', ['b', 'c']]]`` → paths: ``['a']``, ``['a', 'b']``, ``['a', 'b', "
"'c']`` (a nested list is a child that has children of its own)"
msgstr ""
"``[['a', ['b', 'c']]]`` → chemins : ``['a']``, ``['a', 'b']``, ``['a', "
"'b', 'c']`` (une liste imbriquée est un enfant qui a lui-même des "
"enfants)"

msgid "Standard view for iterating over paths"
msgstr "Vue standard pour itérer sur les chemins"

msgid ":py:obj:`expand_structure`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`expand_structure`"

msgid "Static method to expand a compact structure"
msgstr "Méthode statique pour développer une structure compacte"

msgid ""
"Iteration, membership, filtering and navigation work as on "
":class:`~ndict_tools.PathsView`. The members specific to the compact "
"representation are :attr:`structure`, :meth:`expand`, "
":meth:`expand_structure`, :meth:`is_covering`, :meth:`coverage`, "
":meth:`missing_paths` and :meth:`uncovered_paths`."
msgstr ""
"L’itération, l’appartenance, le filtrage et la navigation fonctionnent "
"comme sur :class:`~ndict_tools.PathsView`. Les membres propres à la "
"représentation compacte sont :attr:`structure`, :meth:`expand`, "
":meth:`expand_structure`, :meth:`is_covering`, :meth:`coverage`, "
":meth:`missing_paths` et :meth:`uncovered_paths`."

msgid "Convert this CompactPathsView to a PathsView."
msgstr "Convertit ce CompactPathsView en PathsView."

msgid "Standard paths view with the same underlying data"
msgstr "Vue standard des chemins, sur les mêmes données sous-jacentes"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> cpaths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> paths = cpaths.to_paths()\n"
">>> type(paths).__name__\n"
"'PathsView'"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> cpaths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> paths = cpaths.to_paths()\n"
">>> type(paths).__name__\n"
"'PathsView'"

msgid "Return a new CompactPathsView on the same nested dictionary."
msgstr "Renvoie un nouveau CompactPathsView sur le même dictionnaire imbriqué."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> cpaths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2}).compact_paths()\n"
">>> compact = cpaths.to_compact()\n"
">>> type(compact).__name__\n"
"'CompactPathsView'\n"
">>> compact.structure == cpaths.structure\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> cpaths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2}).compact_paths()\n"
">>> compact = cpaths.to_compact()\n"
">>> type(compact).__name__\n"
"'CompactPathsView'\n"
">>> compact.structure == cpaths.structure\n"
"True"

msgid ""
"Calculate the share of the paths of a nested dictionary found in this "
"view."
msgstr ""
"Calcule la part des chemins d’un dictionnaire imbriqué présents dans "
"cette vue."

msgid ""
"With S the set of paths expanded from this structure and T the set of "
"paths of ``stacked_dict``, coverage is ``len(S & T) / len(T)``. Paths of "
"S that are not in T do not change it, so the value stays between 0.0 and "
"1.0. When T is empty, the result is 1.0 if S is empty too and 0.0 "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Avec S l’ensemble des chemins développés à partir de cette structure et T"
" l’ensemble des chemins de ``stacked_dict``, la couverture vaut ``len(S &"
" T) / len(T)``. Les chemins de S absents de T ne la modifient pas ; la "
"valeur reste donc comprise entre 0.0 et 1.0. Lorsque T est vide, le "
"résultat vaut 1.0 si S est vide aussi, et 0.0 sinon."

msgid "The nested dictionary to compare against (any class of the family)"
msgstr ""
"Le dictionnaire imbriqué de comparaison (de n’importe quelle classe de la"
" famille)"

msgid "Coverage between 0.0 and 1.0"
msgstr "Couverture comprise entre 0.0 et 1.0"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> c_paths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.coverage(nd)\n"
"1.0"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> c_paths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.coverage(nd)\n"
"1.0"

msgid ""
">>> # Partial coverage: only 'a' and 'a.b' out of 4 paths\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a', 'b']]\n"
">>> c_paths.coverage(nd)\n"
"0.5"
msgstr ""
">>> # Couverture partielle : seulement 'a' et 'a.b' sur 4 chemins\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a', 'b']]\n"
">>> c_paths.coverage(nd)\n"
"0.5"

msgid ""
">>> # Extra paths do not raise the value above 1.0\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a', 'b', 'c'], ['d'], ['e']]\n"
">>> c_paths.coverage(nd)\n"
"1.0"
msgstr ""
">>> # Des chemins en trop ne portent pas la valeur au-delà de 1.0\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a', 'b', 'c'], ['d'], ['e']]\n"
">>> c_paths.coverage(nd)\n"
"1.0"

msgid ""
"For a view created from the nested dictionary it is compared with: "
"``nd.compact_paths().coverage(nd)`` always returns 1.0 because all paths "
"from nd are included."
msgstr ""
"Pour une vue créée à partir du dictionnaire imbriqué auquel on la compare"
" : ``nd.compact_paths().coverage(nd)`` renvoie toujours 1.0, car tous les"
" chemins de nd sont inclus."

msgid ""
"Use ``missing_paths()`` to list the extra paths and ``is_covering()`` to "
"check that the two sets are equal."
msgstr ""
"Utilisez ``missing_paths()`` pour énumérer les chemins en trop et "
"``is_covering()`` pour vérifier que les deux ensembles sont égaux."

msgid "Expand this instance's compact structure to full paths."
msgstr "Développe la structure compacte de cette instance en chemins complets."

msgid "All expanded paths"
msgstr "Tous les chemins développés"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> c_paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}}).compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b']]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> c_paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}}).compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b']]"

msgid ""
"This is equivalent to calling expand_structure(self.structure), and "
"should give the same result as list(self) from the parent class."
msgstr ""
"Équivaut à appeler expand_structure(self.structure), et doit donner le "
"même résultat que list(self) de la classe parente."

msgid "Expand compact structure back to full paths."
msgstr "Développe une structure compacte en chemins complets."

msgid ""
"This is the inverse operation of compactification. Several structures can"
" expand to the same paths; the structure built from a dictionary is the "
"canonical one, and each set of paths has exactly one canonical structure."
msgstr ""
"C’est l’opération inverse de la factorisation. Plusieurs structures "
"peuvent se développer en les mêmes chemins ; la structure construite à "
"partir d’un dictionnaire est la structure canonique, et chaque ensemble "
"de chemins a exactement une structure canonique."

msgid "Compact structure to expand"
msgstr "Structure compacte à développer"

msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import CompactPathsView\n"
">>> structure = ['a', ['b', 'c', 'd']]\n"
">>> CompactPathsView.expand_structure(structure)\n"
"[['a'], ['b'], ['b', 'c'], ['b', 'd']]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import CompactPathsView\n"
">>> structure = ['a', ['b', 'c', 'd']]\n"
">>> CompactPathsView.expand_structure(structure)\n"
"[['a'], ['b'], ['b', 'c'], ['b', 'd']]"

msgid ""
">>> # Inside a node list, a nested list is a chain, not siblings\n"
">>> CompactPathsView.expand_structure([['b', ['c', 'd']]])\n"
"[['b'], ['b', 'c'], ['b', 'c', 'd']]"
msgstr ""
">>> # Dans une liste de nœud, une liste imbriquée est une chaîne, pas des"
" nœuds frères\n"
">>> CompactPathsView.expand_structure([['b', ['c', 'd']]])\n"
"[['b'], ['b', 'c'], ['b', 'c', 'd']]"

msgid ""
">>> structure = [['x', ['y', 'z1', 'z2'], 'a']]\n"
">>> CompactPathsView.expand_structure(structure)\n"
"[['x'], ['x', 'y'], ['x', 'y', 'z1'], ['x', 'y', 'z2'], ['x', 'a']]"
msgstr ""
">>> structure = [['x', ['y', 'z1', 'z2'], 'a']]\n"
">>> CompactPathsView.expand_structure(structure)\n"
"[['x'], ['x', 'y'], ['x', 'y', 'z1'], ['x', 'y', 'z2'], ['x', 'a']]"

msgid "Check if this view describes exactly the paths of a nested dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Teste si cette vue décrit exactement les chemins d’un dictionnaire "
"imbriqué."

msgid ""
"With S the set of paths expanded from this structure and T the set of "
"paths of ``stacked_dict``, the result is ``S == T``. It is stricter than "
"full coverage: ``coverage()`` returns ``1.0`` as soon as T is included in"
" S, while ``is_covering()`` also requires S to hold no other path."
msgstr ""
"Avec S l’ensemble des chemins développés à partir de cette structure et T"
" l’ensemble des chemins de ``stacked_dict``, le résultat est ``S == T``. "
"C’est plus strict qu’une couverture complète : ``coverage()`` renvoie "
"``1.0`` dès que T est inclus dans S, tandis que ``is_covering()`` exige "
"en plus que S ne contienne aucun autre chemin."

msgid "True if both sets of paths are equal"
msgstr "True si les deux ensembles de chemins sont égaux"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> c_paths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.is_covering(nd)\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2})\n"
">>> c_paths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.is_covering(nd)\n"
"True"

msgid ""
">>> # Partial coverage\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a']]  # Only covers 'a', not 'a.b' or 'c'\n"
">>> c_paths.is_covering(nd)\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> # Couverture partielle\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a']]  # Ne couvre que 'a', ni 'a.b' ni 'c'\n"
">>> c_paths.is_covering(nd)\n"
"False"

msgid ""
">>> # Every path of nd plus an extra one: full coverage, not equal\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a', 'b'], 'c', 'e']\n"
">>> c_paths.coverage(nd), c_paths.is_covering(nd)\n"
"(1.0, False)"
msgstr ""
">>> # Tous les chemins de nd et un de plus : couverture totale, sans "
"égalité\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a', 'b'], 'c', 'e']\n"
">>> c_paths.coverage(nd), c_paths.is_covering(nd)\n"
"(1.0, False)"

msgid ""
"For a view created from the nested dictionary it is compared with: "
"``nd.compact_paths().is_covering(nd)`` always returns True because the "
"compact structure is built from all paths in nd."
msgstr ""
"Pour une vue créée à partir du dictionnaire imbriqué auquel on la compare"
" : ``nd.compact_paths().is_covering(nd)`` renvoie toujours True, car la "
"structure compacte est construite à partir de tous les chemins de nd."

msgid "Get paths from this view that are NOT in the nested dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie les chemins de cette vue qui ne sont PAS dans le dictionnaire "
"imbriqué."

msgid ""
"Returns the list of paths that exist in this view's expanded form but do "
"not exist in the target nested dictionary. Useful for identifying extra "
"or invalid paths."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie la liste des chemins présents dans la forme développée de cette "
"vue mais absents du dictionnaire imbriqué cible. Utile pour repérer les "
"chemins en trop ou invalides."

msgid "list of paths in this view but not in stacked_dict"
msgstr "liste des chemins présents dans cette vue mais pas dans stacked_dict"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> c_paths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.missing_paths(nd)\n"
"[]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1}})\n"
">>> c_paths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.missing_paths(nd)\n"
"[]"

msgid ""
">>> # Add extra paths\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a', 'b', 'c'], ['d']]\n"
">>> c_paths.missing_paths(nd)\n"
"[['a', 'c'], ['d']]"
msgstr ""
">>> # Ajoute des chemins en trop\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a', 'b', 'c'], ['d']]\n"
">>> c_paths.missing_paths(nd)\n"
"[['a', 'c'], ['d']]"

msgid ""
"For a view created from the nested dictionary it is compared with: "
"``nd.compact_paths().missing_paths(nd)`` always returns [] because all "
"paths are derived from nd."
msgstr ""
"Pour une vue créée à partir du dictionnaire imbriqué auquel on la compare"
" : ``nd.compact_paths().missing_paths(nd)`` renvoie toujours [], car tous"
" les chemins proviennent de nd."

msgid ":py:obj:`uncovered_paths`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`uncovered_paths`"

msgid "Get paths in the nested dictionary not covered by this view"
msgstr "Renvoie les chemins du dictionnaire imbriqué non couverts par cette vue"

msgid "Get the compact structure representation."
msgstr "Renvoie la représentation en structure compacte."

msgid "Compact representation as nested lists"
msgstr "Représentation compacte sous forme de listes imbriquées"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> c_paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}}).compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.structure\n"
"[['a', 'b', 'c']]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> c_paths = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}}).compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.structure\n"
"[['a', 'b', 'c']]"

msgid "Get paths from the nested dictionary that are NOT covered by this view."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie les chemins du dictionnaire imbriqué qui ne sont PAS couverts par"
" cette vue."

msgid ""
"Returns the list of paths that exist in the target nested dictionary but "
"are not present in this view's expanded form. Useful for identifying gaps"
" in coverage."
msgstr ""
"Renvoie la liste des chemins présents dans le dictionnaire imbriqué cible"
" mais absents de la forme développée de cette vue. Utile pour repérer les"
" lacunes de la couverture."

msgid "list of paths in stacked_dict but not in this view"
msgstr "liste des chemins présents dans stacked_dict mais pas dans cette vue"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> c_paths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.uncovered_paths(nd)\n"
"[]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({'a': {'b': 1, 'c': 2}, 'd': 3})\n"
">>> c_paths = nd.compact_paths()\n"
">>> c_paths.uncovered_paths(nd)\n"
"[]"

msgid ""
">>> # Partial structure\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a', 'b']]\n"
">>> c_paths.uncovered_paths(nd)\n"
"[['a', 'c'], ['d']]"
msgstr ""
">>> # Structure partielle\n"
">>> c_paths.structure = [['a', 'b']]\n"
">>> c_paths.uncovered_paths(nd)\n"
"[['a', 'c'], ['d']]"

msgid ""
"For a view created from the nested dictionary it is compared with: "
"``nd.compact_paths().uncovered_paths(nd)`` always returns [] because all "
"paths from nd are included."
msgstr ""
"Pour une vue créée à partir du dictionnaire imbriqué auquel on la compare"
" : ``nd.compact_paths().uncovered_paths(nd)`` renvoie toujours [], car "
"tous les chemins de nd sont inclus."

msgid ":py:obj:`missing_paths`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`missing_paths`"

msgid "Get paths in this view not in the nested dictionary"
msgstr "Renvoie les chemins de cette vue absents du dictionnaire imbriqué"

msgid ":py:obj:`coverage`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`coverage`"

msgid "Get coverage ratio"
msgstr "Renvoie le taux de couverture"

